[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ## Requirements

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 1. The application

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  Created with `rails new`, with the two flags that decide the rest of the semester: PostgreSQL as the
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  database, and Bootstrap as the CSS framework. Both are chosen at creation time.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - `bin/rails about` reports **Rails 8** and the **PostgreSQL** adapter. An application on SQLite does
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    not meet this requirement, whatever else it does.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The development and test databases exist, and the application connects to them.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - `Gemfile.lock`, `package.json` and the lock file your package manager wrote are committed.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  > The application starts with **`bin/dev`**. `bin/rails server` also starts it, and does not rebuild
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  > your CSS.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 2. Routes

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  Four pages, four routes, declared in `config/routes.rb`:

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  | The page | What it is for |
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  |---|---|
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  | Home | What Wheelhouse is, and the way in to the other three |
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  | Services | The list from the wall: every job the shop does, with its price |
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  | Visiting the workshop | Where the shop is, when it is open, what happens when you bring a bike in |
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  | About | Who runs the shop |

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - Home is the **root route**. Opening the application at `/` must not show the Rails welcome page.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The other three answer at readable paths of your choosing.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - Every route is **named**, and every link is written with its route helper. A hard-coded
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    `href="/services"` does not meet this requirement.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - `bin/rails routes` lists exactly what the application answers to: nothing declared that leads
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    nowhere, nothing reachable that is not declared. What `rails new` put in that file stays — the
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    health check at `/up` is used in Class 14.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 3. The controller

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  **One controller, written by hand**, with one action per page. Create the file yourself, and the
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  view files with it.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The action for the services page prepares the jobs and their prices and hands them to the view in an
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    instance variable, written **in Ruby, in the controller** — an array of hashes, or whatever shape
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    you prefer. In Lab 5 that list becomes a table and its seed data.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - Nothing here touches a database. There is no database to touch yet.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 4. The pages

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  The content comes from your Lab 3 documents, and from the owner's description they came from.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **The services page lists at least twelve jobs**, and the view builds the list by iterating over the
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    collection the controller gave it. Twelve rows typed into the template do not meet this requirement,
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    and it is checked by changing the array and reloading.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - Every page has one `h1`, and the outline below it does not skip levels. Templating the HTML does not
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    change what Lab 1 required of it.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **Nothing on these pages is a customer, a bicycle or a repair.** The owner was explicit: the price
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    list is public and nothing else is.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 5. The layout

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  `app/views/layouts/application.html.erb` holds what every page shares; each view holds only the part
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  that changes.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The doctype, `<html>`, `<head>` and the navigation appear **once, in the layout**. A view that
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    contains any of them does not meet this requirement.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The navigation is a **Bootstrap navbar**, links to all four pages, and collapses to a toggle on a
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    narrow screen.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The navbar **marks which page you are currently on**. Rails has a helper that answers that question;
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    find it in the guides.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 6. Bootstrap, compiled and made yours

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **Bootstrap is the one you installed**, compiled from Sass into `app/assets/builds/`. A `<link>` to
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    a CDN does not meet this requirement.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The pages use it for real: the navbar, its **grid** for at least one region that is several columns
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    wide on a laptop and one on a phone, and its table or list components for the price list.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **At least two Bootstrap Sass variables are overridden** in
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    `app/assets/stylesheets/application.bootstrap.scss`, visibly. Where the override goes relative to
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    the Bootstrap import decides whether it does anything; the Bootstrap documentation explains why.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - The site is usable at **375px** and at **1280px**, with no horizontal scrolling at either width.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 7. The README

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  The README is the front door of the project for the rest of the semester, and it is graded on one
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  criterion: **someone who has never seen your repository can clone it and get it running by following
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  only the README.**

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  At minimum: what Wheelhouse is and links to the documents in `docs/`; the prerequisites with their
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  versions; the setup commands in the order they must be run; and how to start the application.

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  ### 8. What you may not do

[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **No models, no migrations, no tables.** There is not one migration in the repository at the end of
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    this lab. Lab 5 turns your Lab 3 diagram into a schema, and starting today means starting it twice.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **Nothing written for you.** The controller and the views are files you created yourself.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **No `resources`.** Declare the four routes one by one.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **No Bootstrap from a CDN**, and no second CSS framework.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **No SQLite.**
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **Nothing generated in the repository**: not `node_modules/`, not `app/assets/builds/`, and not
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    `config/master.key`. Confirm it on GitHub, not in your editor.
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m  - **No forms that submit anything**, no authentication, no JavaScript of your own. Forms are Class 8,
[34m[49m[29m[28m[27m[25m[25m[1m[24m[22m[1m[23m    authentication is Class 12, and Bootstrap's own JavaScript came with the installation.

